--- body ---
## Context

Commit `4dc99e5` ("prompts: restructure modules to numbered scheme (1-6, A-D)")
renamed the module files under `experiments/prompts/modules/` and edited their
contents, but `experiments/prompts/prompt_complete.txt` was not regenerated
from the new module set. The drift was discovered while merging PR #334
(ticket 0175): `tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py` fails because
content lines in `prompt_complete.txt` no longer match the assembled
composite of `modules/*.txt`.

In PR #334 the failing test was marked `@pytest.mark.skip` so the suite would
stay green while ticket 0175 landed the harness rewrite. The skip is
technical debt: that adherence test is the regression guard that *would have*
caught harness.py reading `base.txt` after the rename. Without re-enabling
it, future module-rename drift will go undetected the same way.

## Actions

1. Regenerate `experiments/prompts/prompt_complete.txt` from the current
   module set via the new `assemble_prompt(modules_dir, names)` contract.
   Either:
   - Add a small Make target that writes the assembled composite, or
   - Run a one-off script and check the result in.
   The composite must use the ALWAYS_MODULES pair (`2_goal`, `5_table`)
   plus the canonical optional modules (`1_persona`, `3_overview`,
   `4_narratives`, `6_bibliography`, `A_Statistics`, `B_Temporality`,
   `C_Uncertainty`, `D_Completeness`) — matching
   `sweep_ablation_p1_direct_composite` in `experiments/experiments.toml`.

2. Un-skip `tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py`: remove the
   `@pytest.mark.skip(...)` decorator. Keep `@pytest.mark.adherence`.

3. Verify the test asserts the right invariant under the new always-pair
   contract. If `assemble_prompt` always injects `2_goal + 5_table`, the
   test must call `assemble_prompt` with the full module list explicitly
   (not rely on an "all modules" globbing path that no longer exists in
   harness.py) — adapt accordingly.

4. (Optional, recommended) Add a Make rule so `prompt_complete.txt` is a
   build artifact regenerated from `modules/*.txt`, with a stamp file or
   direct dependency. This converts the adherence test from a periodic
   audit into a build-time invariant.

## Test

```python
@pytest.mark.adherence
def test_modules_cover_prompt_complete():
    from aedist.harness import assemble_prompt
    modules_dir = EXPERIMENTS_DIR / "prompts" / "modules"
    prompt_complete = (EXPERIMENTS_DIR / "prompts" / "prompt_complete.txt").read_text()
    all_stems = sorted(p.stem for p in modules_dir.glob("*.txt"))
    assembled = assemble_prompt(modules_dir, all_stems)
    assert _content_lines(prompt_complete) == _content_lines(assembled)
```

## Exit criteria

- `experiments/prompts/prompt_complete.txt` matches the assembled output of
  the canonical composite module list (modulo blank-line / header whitespace).
- `pytest tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py` runs (not skips) and
  passes.
- No `@pytest.mark.skip` decorator remains in
  `tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py`.
- `make check-fast` and `make check` both pass.

## Reference

Follow-up from PR #334 (ticket 0175). See PR description "Out of scope"
section and the file docstring of `tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py`.
